Short:        HTTPS downloader with TLS 1.3, no deps
Author:       Stefan "Bebbo" Franke <s.franke@bebbosoft.de>
Uploader:     Michele Dipace <michele.dipace@kaffeine.net>
Type:         comm/net
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH_TOKEN@

bebboget for AROS @TARGET_SHORT@
==============================================================================

bebboget gets files from HTTPS and HTTP servers. It only needs
bsdsocket.library, the AROS TCP/IP stack, and supports TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3.
installcerts installs root certificates from a PEM bundle.

This is my AROS port of bebboget by Stefan "Bebbo" Franke. His Amiga version
is comm/net/bebboget.lha on Aminet.

This archive is for @TARGET_LONG@.
The builds for the other AROS targets (i386, x86_64, aarch64) are separate
archives.

==============================================================================
INSTALL

Copy the two programs to C: or to another directory in the path:

    Copy bebboget installcerts C:

bebboget keeps a random seed in ENVARC:bebboget/random_seed.

==============================================================================
CERTIFICATES

bebboget comes without certificates. For a server it cannot verify it asks
at the console: (a)bort, (i)nstall or (c)ontinue. To install the root
certificates of the curl CA bundle once:

    bebboget --sloppy -D RAM: -o cacert.pem https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem
    installcerts RAM:cacert.pem

--sloppy skips the certificate checks for that download. If you prefer, copy
cacert.pem from a machine you trust instead.

The certificates go to SYS:Prefs/Env-Archive/certs.

==============================================================================
USAGE

    bebboget [options] <url>

For example:

    bebboget -D RAM: https://aminet.net/comm/net/bebboget.readme

bebboget -? lists the options. Ctrl-C stops a download. A download that ends
before its Content-Length is reported and returns 10.

==============================================================================
KNOWN LIMITS

- The HTTP status is not checked: an error page from the server is saved as
  the file.
- TLS 1.2 has no ECDHE-ECDSA cipher suites: such servers need TLS 1.3.
- A server whose chain ends in a cross-signed root that is no longer in the
  bundle needs a confirmation at the console (www.google.com today).
- Errors such as "certificate not accepted" return 0.
@ARCH_LIMITS@
